  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe current approach uses multi-resolution optimization with SLSQP, which often gets stuck in local optima. The proposed approach uses a genetic algorithm with a repair function to enforce constraints and explores the search space more effectively. The genetic algorithm maintains a population of candidates, applies crossover and mutation, and uses tournament selection to promote diversity. The repair function ensures feasibility by clipping values to [0,1] and adjusting the sum to meet the integral constraint. This method is better suited for non-convex problems with many local minima.\n\nMathematical specification:\n- Representation: h is a vector of length n_points (188) with values in [0,1] and sum n_points/2.\n- Objective: Minimize C5 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx, computed via correlation.\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i, and sum(h) = n_points/2.\n- Repair function: Clips values to [0,1] and adjusts the sum to exactly n_points/2 by scaling or water-filling.\n- Algorithm: Genetic algorithm with tournament selection, simulated binary crossover (SBX), and polynomial mutation.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Define n_points = 188 and dx = 2.0/n_points.\n2. Define repair function to handle clipping and sum adjustment.\n3. Define objective function using np.correlate and repair.\n4. Set bounds [(0,1)] * n_points.\n5. Initialize population with parent solution if available.\n6. Use tournament selection, SBX crossover, and polynomial mutation.\n7. Monitor time and stop if budget exceeded.\n8. Return best candidate and its objective.\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Population size: 100.\n- Crossover probability: 0.9.\n- Mutation probability: 0.1.\n- Tournament size: 5.\n- Repair method: Scaling or water-filling based on sum.\n\nComputebudget and robustness:\n- Time estimate: 110000 evaluations at 0.01s/evaluation = 1100 seconds.\n- Stop if time exceeds budget or no improvement in 100 evaluations.\n- Fallback: Return parent solution if available.\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- Ensure 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 and sum(h) = n_points/2.\n- Recompute objective for best candidate.\n- Return (h_values, c5_bound, n_points).",
